+# Knowledge
+
+Knowledge owns document persistence and exposes the published document catalog through
+`Knowledge::Catalog.list(tenant_id:)`. Consumers must use that API rather than reaching
+into `Knowledge::Document` or its tables.
+
+## Persistence rollback
+
+Before any future persistence conversion, take a verified database backup and record the
+current application revision. Deploy the conversion behind a reversible cutover: stop
+new writes, restore the backup (or switch back to the prior schema/code), and replay or
+reconcile only from the authoritative documents and revisions. Verify tenant scoping,
+publication state, IDs, bodies, and revisions with the characterization tests before
+resuming delivery. This extraction makes no persistence conversion.
